ich a CNN can classify images, often measured in images per second.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Speedups of convolution layers': {'type': ['method', 'task', 'generic'], 'description': ['The improvement in processing speed achieved by the optimized sparse CNN implementation, specifically 3.4x and 7.3x on Xeon and Atom processors, respectively, compared to the best dense direct convolution performance.', 'The objective of achieving performance improvements in the convolution layers of AlexNet, specifically 3.4x and 7.3x speedups on Xeon and Atom processors, respectively.', 'The performance improvement achieved in convolution layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3, 3]}, 'Overhead of transforming tensors to matrices': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The computational cost associated with converting tensors into matrices in sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Direct sparse convolution algorithm': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['An algorithm designed to perform sparse convolution operations efficiently.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'SpMDM (sparse matrix and dense matrix multiplication)': {'type': ['GENERIC', 'method'], 'description': ['A method for performing matrix multiplication with sparse matrices.', 'A method used for implementing fully connected layers, leveraging sparse matrix multiplication to exploit sparsity.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 5]}, 'Dense convolution': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['Standard convolution operations performed on dense data.', 'A standard convolution operation that uses dense weight tensors.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 5]}, 'Perforated-CNN': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A CNN variant that improves classification speed in convolution layers by eliminating redundant computations, relying on interpolation instead of sparse methods.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'GEMM': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['General Matrix Multiplication, a fundamental operation used in implementing fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Speedup': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The improvement in processing speed achieved by using sparse convolution compared to dense convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Weight tensor': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A multi-dimensional array of weights used in convolutional layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'FLOP/s': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Floating point operations per second, a measure of computational performance.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Bottleneck': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['A component or layer in a neural network that limits the overall processing speed, often becoming a performance constraint after optimizations in other areas, such as sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Holistic SparseCNN': {'type': ['GENERIC', 'GENERIC'], 'description': ['A method for optimizing CNNs by simultaneously considering sparsity in both convolutional and fully connected layers.', 'A novel method that simultaneously optimizes both fully connected and convolution layers in CNNs to improve speed, reduce size, and maintain accuracy.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'Weight decay': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['A regularization technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty to the loss function based on the magnitude of the weights.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'BDW': {'type': ['GENERIC'], 'description': ['A hardware platform where the Holistic SparseCNN achieved a classification speed of 2,371 images per second.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 1e-5': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific regularization parameter used for weight decay in the fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 5e-5': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific regularization parameter used for weight decay in the fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 6e-5': {'type': 