ed and convolution layers to reduce model size and accelerate classification speed.\n', 'Name:CONVOLUTION LAYERS\nDescription:The compute-heavy parts of CNNs. ; Layers in a CNN that apply convolutional filters to the input data. ; Layers within a CNN that perform the majority of the computation (FLOPS) and are targeted for sparsity to improve classification speed. ; Fundamental component of CNNs, responsible for feature extraction. The text discusses optimizing their speed. ; The focus of sparse CNN research, aimed at optimizing the speed of these layers within the network. ; Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations, crucial for feature extraction. ; Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations, a key component for feature extraction. ; Layers in a CNN that apply convolutional filters to the input data. ; A fundamental component of CNNs, where the Holistic SparseCNN method is applied to improve performance.\n', 'Name:PRUNING\nDescription:A technique used to reduce the size and computational complexity of a neural network by removing less important connections or weights. In this context, it is applied to CNNs to improve inference speed and reduce model size.\n', 'Name:IMPROVE INFERENCE SPEED\nDescription:The objective of optimizing Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) to reduce the time taken for making predictions.\n']split_entities: text_tokens=1893, instructions_tokens=500, budget_for_entities=7607, number_of_entities=59, avg_entity_tokens=56, max_entities=135, num_groups=1, entities_per_group=[59]
